[{:seon.task/name "a-long-string-does-not-starve-its-siblings"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-10-21 by session AGENTS: an eval item {:form \"(code-of 0)\" :out <9,600 chars of pprint output> :value (vec (range 2000))} printed under 545 tokens (seon.print/print-value, the last-evals share) shows 1,584 characters of :out and :value as `[…2000 (get-in (nth (my.turn/evals) 0) [:value])]`: not one element of the value the agent asked for. Cause: seon.print.select ranks a long string before a collection (member-rank, select.clj:109-118) and then the string's characters are allotted like one member, greedily, while the collection's members are a level deeper, so breadth-first never reaches them. Correct: a long string's characters are allotted in the same rounds as its siblings' members (a string is a sequence of lines for allotment), so every sibling shows its first part before any one deepens. A general printer improvement: every value with a long string beside a collection benefits (contract refusals, test expected/actual, the context). Replaces nothing; the law tests in seon.print-test stay green."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/a-long-string-shares-the-budget-with-its-siblings}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-long-name-is-cut-like-any-text"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root's review of worktree session printer-eval (jolt/printer-eval): since the one string cutter (`seon.print.select/break-at`, `seon.print.emit/cut-words`), a string in a value and prose both cut as `\"prefix\"…+7279 chars in 88 more lines (subs result/h3 19523)`, but a keyword or symbol longer than :seon.config.render.agent/max-name still prints a bare `prefix…+N` with no unit and no form (`seon.print.select/tree-node`'s :name row; `seon.print.select/node-continuation` names no form for a name). Blind scoring on the printer-eval corpus ranked the bare `…+N` last most often (notes/printer-eval/README.md: no unit). Correct: a name's cut says `…+N chars` and names the form that reads the whole name (`(str (get-in result/h3 path))`, or `(name …)`), through the same cut words; the print-test laws then require a form on every cut through a handle with no exception for names. Replaces the name row's own cut text."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/the-text-stays-inside-its-budget}}]
